Z||000033||Ken Wittlief||06-15-2001||03:30 PM||||I've been stewing over the best movie thing for a few days<P>I think it should be a film that affected your life somehow, you went in, saw the film, came out, and your life was different for the experience.<P>  only one I can come up with is (Cornball alert!!!) Groundhog Day<P>  first time I saw it, it was just funny - but after seeing it a few times, it grows on you, esp the part " you wake up every morning and your life is exactly the same as it was yeasterday, and there is nothing you can do about it" - that is so profound - given the rest of the flick.<P>  another test for a great movie would be one you can watch when you are feeling down or a little off, and it takes your mind off things for a while, or lifts your spirits.<P>  for that.... _________________?!?! drawing a blank on this one.<P>  since I cant attribute these qualities to a whole bunch of movies, Im afraid that says something about hollywood.||||reg||1
